I have a complete picture. Here's the report.

---

# Twyne research / "Apparatus" subsystem

## 1. The research provider abstraction

There are **two distinct provider layers**, and the naming is a bit subtle:

### Layer A — `ApparatusResearchProvider`: *which route the search takes*

Defined in `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/types/index.ts:917`:

```ts
export type ApparatusResearchProvider =
  | "hosted"
  | "search-api"
  | "model-web-search"
  | "web-mcp";
```

with the doc comment:

> `hosted:` Twyne's own service, using the server's provider key. `search-api:` a search API called straight from this browser (BYOK), configured by `searchBackend`. `model-web-search:` the writer's own model provider, with web search on. `web-mcp:` tools discovered from the writer's MCP servers.

Stored in `ApparatusSettings` (`src/types/index.ts:~995`):

```ts
export interface ApparatusSettings {
  defaultCitationStyle: ApparatusCitationStyle;
  aiEnhanceCitations: boolean;
  flagMissingSources: boolean;
  autoInsertFootnotes: boolean;
  researchProvider: ApparatusResearchProvider;
  searchBackend: SearchBackendConfig;
  maxResults: number;              // sources requested per claim
  mcpServers: McpServerConfig[];
}
```

Default is `researchProvider: "hosted"`, `maxResults: 8`.

### Layer B — `SearchBackendAdapter`: *which vendor answers a BYOK search*

`/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/utils/research-backends.ts` — this is the clean pluggable interface:

```ts
export interface SearchRequest {
  query: string;
  context: string;
  maxResults: number;
}

export interface SearchBackendAdapter {
  id: SearchBackendId;
  label: string;
  /** Shown in settings so the writer knows where to get a key. */
  keyHint: string;
  defaultUrl: string;
  /** Whether the writer must supply their own endpoint. */
  requiresUrl?: boolean;
  buildRequest(req: SearchRequest, config: SearchBackendConfig): { url: string; init: RequestInit };
  /** Pull the result array out of the parsed response body. */
  extract(body: unknown, config: SearchBackendConfig): unknown;
}
```

`SearchBackendId = "tinyfish" | "exa" | "tavily" | "brave" | "serper" | "custom"` (`src/types/index.ts:~926`). **TinyFish is the default** (`DEFAULT_SEARCH_BACKEND = { id: "tinyfish", apiKey: "", baseUrl: "", resultsPath: "" }`), endpoint `https://api.search.tinyfish.ai/v1/search`. `searchBackend(id)` falls back to `SEARCH_BACKENDS.tinyfish` for unknown ids.

Adding a vendor is one entry in `SEARCH_BACKENDS`. `toSource()` / `toSources()` normalize any vendor shape into `Source` by reading every common field spelling (`title|name|heading`, `snippet|description|text|content|summary|excerpt`, etc.), require an `http(s)` URL, dedupe by URL, truncate snippets at 1200 chars. `runSearchBackend()` is the entry point.

### The hosted path (server-side)

`/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/convex/research.ts` (`"use node"`). Header states the whole contract:

```
searchSources({ query, context }) -> { results: Source[] }
fetchSource  ({ url })            -> { title, author, …, markdown, embeddable }
```

Canonical types:

```ts
export interface Source {
  title: string;
  url: string;
  snippet: string;
  author?: string;
  publisher?: string;
  date?: string;
  why?: string;
}

export interface FetchedSource {
  title: string;
  author?: string;
  publisher?: string;
  date?: string;
  markdown: string;
  embeddable: boolean;
}
```

A server-side `ProviderSpec` table mirrors the client adapters (`tinyfish | exa | tavily | brave | serper | custom`), selected by env: `RESEARCH_PROVIDER` (default `"tinyfish"`), `RESEARCH_API_KEY` (falls back to `TINYFISH_API_KEY`), `RESEARCH_SEARCH_URL`, `RESEARCH_FETCH_URL`. TinyFish is the only provider with a distinct fetch endpoint baked in (`https://api.fetch.tinyfish.ai/v1/fetch`, `format: "markdown"`).

Both actions are rate-limited (`consumeRateLimit` with `RATE_LIMITS.research` for Pro, `RATE_LIMITS.researchFree` otherwise) and return `provider: "local"` with a deterministic stub when signed out or unkeyed. The client explicitly **rejects** the local stub as evidence (`background-research.ts:~685`): *"local placeholder results are not fact-check evidence."*

Note: `fetchSource` is defined but has **no caller in `src/`** — only `searchSources` is invoked (`background-research.ts:681`). The apparatus route has `embedUrl/embedMarkdown/embedProvider` store fields, so the URL→markdown reader is wired in the UI store but the action call isn't reachable from the search I ran; worth a closer look if you need it.

---

## 2. How research is triggered from the editor

### The background watcher — "research while writing"

`/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/utils/background-research.ts` (861 lines) is the engine. Its header describes the loop: watch the folio (debounced) → AI extracts `ResearchTarget`s → dedupe → resolve each through the configured provider → merge into bibliography with `provenance: "background"` → stream progress.

Constants worth knowing:
```ts
const DEBOUNCE_MS = 45_000;
const PASS_TTL_MS = 5 * 60_000;        // don't chase the same claims every pass
const MAX_BACKGROUND_PER_FOLIO = 25;   // soft cap
const SNIPPET_MIN_CHARS = 40;
const MIN_DRAFT_CHARS = 120;
const MAX_TARGETS_PER_PASS = 5;        // matches free hosted tier: 5 searches/min
```

Public API: `startBackgroundResearch({ client, brief, folioId })`, `onDraftChanged(text)`, `kickBackgroundResearch(text)`, `stopBackgroundResearch()`, `retryBackgroundResearch()`, `retryResearchTarget(key)`, `researchSelection(req)`, `steerBackgroundResearch(instructions)`, `snapshot()`.

Wired from `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/routes/editor/index.tsx`: `startBackgroundResearch` at line 738, `kickBackgroundResearch(plain)` at 743 (if >40 chars), `onDraftChanged(...)` at 592 on every content event, `stopBackgroundResearch()` at 723/763/794/1323 on folio switch/teardown.

Ownership safety: a module-level `researchGeneration` counter invalidates in-flight passes on folio switch, since providers aren't all abortable.

### The unit of research

`src/types/index.ts:504`:

```ts
export type ResearchTargetKind =
  | "quote" | "work" | "person" | "statistic" | "claim" | "event";

export interface ResearchTarget {
  id: string;            // stable for the pass (UI keys, not persistence)
  kind: ResearchTargetKind;
  anchor: string;        // the passage verbatim as it appears in the draft
  reason: string;        // why this should not stand uncited
  query: string;         // the precise query the search providers receive
  importance: number;    // 1 (nice-to-have) to 5 (argument collapses without it)
}

export interface ResearchTargetRef {
  kind: ResearchTargetKind;
  anchor: string;
  query: string;
  reason?: string;
}
```

Prompting/selection helpers live in `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/utils/research-targets.ts`: `buildResearchExtractSystemPrompt`, `buildResearchExtractUserPrompt`, `parseResearchTargets`, `targetKey`, `selectFreshTargets`, `rankSourcesForTarget`, `buildDossierResearchInstructions`, `dossierResearchMode` (`"fiction" | "nonfiction" | "general"`), `DEFAULT_TARGETS_PER_PASS = 12`, `DRAFT_SCAN_MAX_CHARS = 18_000`.

### Context-sensitive editor popup — "Get sources"

`/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/components/editor/selection-actions.tsx` — a manuscript-anchored floating card that appears on text selection with three actions: **Get sources**, **Add margin**, **Send to persona**. State type in `src/components/editor/editor-state.ts:85`:

```ts
export interface SelectionActionState {
  from: number;
  to: number;
  text: string;
  /** Fixed viewport coordinates; the component centers itself on x. */
  x: number;
  y: number;
  placement: "above" | "below";
  error: string | null;
}
```

The card uses `preventdefault:mousedown` declaratively (a Qwik `onMouseDown$` would run after ProseMirror collapses the range).

Handler `getSourcesForSelection` at `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/components/editor/twyne-editor.tsx:2980` opens the citations panel then calls `researchSelection({ anchor, folioId })`; on failure it writes `result.message` back into `selectionAction.error`, which the card renders inline. Positioning refresh: `refreshSelectionAction` at twyne-editor.tsx:854, rAF-driven at 898/922. Render site: twyne-editor.tsx:3269 (suppressed while a user-comment popover is open).

`researchSelection` (background-research.ts:324) bypasses extraction but reuses provider routing, progress rows, ranking, retry, and persistence. It refuses when the folio changed or a pass is in flight.

### Steering

`/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/components/editorial-board/editorial-board-overlay.tsx:58` calls `steerBackgroundResearch(direction)` — a writer-authored instruction that forces an immediate draft-wide extraction pass.

### Live UI

Two events drive everything: `twyne:background-research` (full snapshot) and `twyne:background-sources` (one claim landed). Consumed by `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/components/citations/citations-panel.tsx:360` (the in-editor "Deep Trace" panel) and `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/routes/apparatus/index.tsx` (the full page).

Progress types (background-research.ts:83-115):

```ts
export type ResearchTargetStatus = "queued" | "searching" | "found" | "missed" | "error";

export interface ResearchProgressItem {
  key: string; kind: string; anchor: string; query: string;
  status: ResearchTargetStatus;
  count?: number; error?: string; at?: number;
}

export interface ResearchActivityEntry {
  id: string; at: number; kind: string; anchor: string; query: string;
  outcome: "found" | "missed" | "error";
  count: number; error?: string;
}
```

Phases surfaced: `"idle" | "extracting" | "searching" | "saving" | "error"`.

---

## 3. Embeddings / vector search / semantic search

**None. There is no embedding, vector, or semantic-search code in this repo.**

- `convex/schema.ts` uses only `.index(...)` — no `.vectorIndex(...)`, no `.searchIndex(...)`. The only `vectorIndex` / `ctx.vectorSearch` hits anywhere are in the vendored doc `convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md:282-293` (Convex's own docs, not app code).
- No `cosine`, `similarity` (as a function), `tf-idf`, `bm25`, `jaccard` implementations. `research-targets.ts:137,168` mentions "topical similarity" only as prompt text telling the model that topical similarity is *not* enough.
- The only "embedding"-adjacent artifacts are **voice embeddings** for the TTS model (`voices/F1.bin` etc. in `browser-inference.ts`) and the phrase "embedding it in a regular expression" in `find-replace.ts:35`.
- Ranking is purely heuristic — `rankSourcesForTarget` in `src/utils/research-targets.ts:373`:

```ts
score:
  (source.snippet && source.snippet.trim().length >= 40 ? 1 : 0) +
  (source.author ? 0.5 : 0) +
  (source.publisher ? 0.5 : 0) +
  (source.title ? 0.25 : 0) +
  Math.max(0, 1 - index * 0.2);   // provider order as a weak prior
```

So a RAG/vector layer would be entirely greenfield.

---

## 4. Where sources / bibliography / documents live

### Bibliography — in the Lix blob, not a Convex table of its own

`/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/utils/bibliography.ts`. Header: persisted at `/bibliography.json` inside the Lix blob (per folio) so it travels with the manuscript.

```ts
const BIB_PATH = "/bibliography.json";
export type BibProvenance = "writer" | "background";

export interface BibEntry {
  id: string;
  folioId: string;
  title: string;
  author?: string; publisher?: string; date?: string;
  year?: string; doi?: string;
  url: string;
  accessedAt: number;
  note?: string;              // writer's working note — never in the citation
  citationKey?: string;       // e.g. "smith2024"
  style?: CitationStyle;
  formattedCitation?: string;
  snippet?: string;
  why?: string;
  pageHint?: string;
  provenance?: BibProvenance;
  backgroundQuery?: string;
  accepted?: boolean;         // writer explicitly accepted a background find
  target?: ResearchTargetRef;
  createdAt?: number;
  citationInsertedAt?: number;
}
```

Helpers: `loadBibliography`, `bibliographyForFolio`, `saveBibliography`, `upsertBibEntry`, `mergeBibEntry`, `deleteBibEntry`, `findBibliographyEntryByUrl`, `normalizeUrl`, plus `formatMla` / `formatApa` / `formatChicago` / `footnoteCite`.

Lix is SQLite-compiled-to-WASM on the main thread (`src/utils/lix.ts:235`), with file paths `/draft.json`, `/brief.json`, `/comments.json`, `/user-comments.json`, `/bibliography.json`, `/folios/${folioId}/brief.json`.

### Convex

`convex/schema.ts:101`:
```ts
bibliographyEntries: defineTable(collectionEntry)
  .index("by_userId", ["userId"])
  .index("by_userId_itemId", ["userId", "itemId"]),
```
where `collectionEntry = { userId, itemId, item: v.any(), order, updatedAt }` — an opaque mirror for sync, not a queryable schema. Related: `folioEntries`, `personaEntries`, `folios`, `folioContent`, `briefs`, `images`, `suggestions`, `personaNotes`. Lix blobs sync via `convex/lixBlobs.ts` / `lixRelay.ts` / `sharedLix.ts`.

### Settings storage

IndexedDB (`DB_NAME = "twyne"`), `src/utils/idb.ts`: `APPARATUS_SETTINGS_STORAGE_KEY = "twyne.apparatus-settings.current"`, meta key `"apparatus-settings"`. `normalizeApparatusSettings` handles the legacy migration `"tinyfish" → "search-api"` and `tinyFishApiKey → searchBackend.apiKey`, `tinyFishMaxResults → maxResults`.

### Is there a local document corpus?

**Not in the sense you mean — no user-downloaded document library.** The nearest thing is **MCP resources treated as a knowledge base**, in `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/utils/mcp-research.ts:410+`:

```ts
export interface McpDocument {
  server: string;
  uri: string;
  title: string;
  mimeType?: string;
  text: string;
}
const MAX_RESOURCE_CHARS = 20_000;
```

`listMcpDocuments(settings, convex)` enumerates resources from servers with `useResources: true` without reading them; `readMcpResource(uri, settings, convex, templateValues)` reads one, text contents only (base64 blobs are skipped as non-citable), truncated to 20k chars. Both are consumed by `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/routes/apparatus/index.tsx`. `McpServerConfig.useResources` is documented as *"Treat this server's resources as citable knowledge-base material."*

The other user-file path is **images only** — `convex/images.ts` + `src/utils/image-upload.ts` (Convex file storage, `images` table with `by_ownerId_folioId`). No PDF/text ingestion, no corpus indexing.

---

## 5. Local / on-device inference

Three separate, already-shipped pieces:

### a) Generic on-device model download/evict — the most reusable primitive

`/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/utils/models-cache.ts`. Header:

> The download-and-evict capability that both the Supertonic voice pack and **any future local model** share. Files land in the IndexedDB `models` store keyed by their remote URL, which lets the transformers.js fetcher be redirected to them […] so inference keeps working offline after the first download.

```ts
export interface ModelFileManifest { url: string; size: number; }
export type ModelDownloadPhase = "not-downloaded" | "downloading" | "ready" | "error";
export interface ModelDownloadState {
  id: string; phase: ModelDownloadPhase;
  downloadedBytes: number; totalBytes: number; progress: number;
  activeFile?: string; error?: string;
}
```
API: `onModelDownload`, `readModelBytes`, `isModelBundleDownloaded`, `modelDownloadState`, `downloadModelBundle`, `evictModelBundle`, `createAbortError`. Backed by `saveModelFileToIdb` / `loadModelFileFromIdb` / `listModelFilesFromIdb` / `deleteModelFileFromIdb` in `src/utils/idb.ts`. Consumers today: `supertonic-tts.ts` and `src/routes/settings/index.tsx`.

### b) transformers.js / ONNX / WebGPU — shipped for TTS

`/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/utils/supertonic-tts.ts` + `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/utils/browser-inference.ts` (deliberately dependency-free so the settings normalizer can import it cheaply; transformers.js stays out of the main bundle).

```ts
export type BrowserTtsDevice = "webgpu" | "wasm" | null;
export type ClientUsageSource = "byok" | "local";

const LOCAL_INFERENCE_PROVIDER_TYPES = new Set<AiProviderConfig["type"]>([
  "litert", "ollama", "supertonic",
]);
```

`browserTtsDevice()` probes `navigator.gpu` then `WebAssembly`. `clientUsageSourceForProvider()` classifies **billing semantics, not transport** — on-device and loopback (`localhost`/`127.0.0.1`/`::1`/`*.localhost`) models count as `"local"` even though LiteRT/Ollama speak OpenAI-compatible HTTP. Model: `onnx-community/Supertonic-TTS-ONNX`, ~263 MB across 9 ONNX files + 9 voice embeddings, `installSupertonicFetchHook()` redirects transformers.js fetches at the IDB cache.

Also WASM-local: Harper grammar (`src/utils/grammar.ts`, `src/components/editor/grammar-panel.tsx:53` — "Harper's local WASM worker") and Lix/SQLite.

### c) Desktop LiteRT + the `eval:local` / free-mode harness

`/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/utils/desktop-bridge.ts` — the Electrobun shell loads `https://twyne.love/?platform=desktop&localAi=1&localPort=<port>`:

```ts
export const LOCAL_MODEL_ID = "gemma-4-e4b";
export const LOCAL_PROVIDER_ID = "desktop-litert-local";
export function localAiBaseUrl(): string | null {  // http://127.0.0.1:<port>/v1
```
`isDesktopLocalAiAvailable()` is the authoritative capability signal (ahead of PostHog flags, which can still be loading at first mount).

`/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/src/utils/feature-flags.ts`:
```ts
/** Surface the desktop-only native LiteRT local model (Gemma 4 E4B). This
 *  only gates the UI; actual availability also requires the Electrobun shell
 *  to advertise a bundled local server. */
localAi: boolean;
// POSTHOG_FEATURE_FLAG_KEYS = { pricing: "twyne-pricing", localAi: "twyne-local-ai" }
```

**`eval:local` harness** — `package.json:57`: `"eval:local": "tsx evals/run-local-model.ts"`. `/home/diogenes/Projects/twyne/evals/run-local-model.ts` header: *"Tool-calling + analysis eval for a small local model (e.g. LFM2.5-2.6B), the candidate engine for signed-out / **free mode**."*

```ts
const BASE_URL = (process.env.LOCAL_MODEL_BASE_URL ?? "http://localhost:8080/v1").replace(/\/$/, "");
const MODEL_ID  = process.env.LOCAL_MODEL_ID  ?? "LFM2.5-2.6B";
const API_KEY   = process.env.LOCAL_MODEL_API_KEY ?? "local";
const TIMEOUT_MS = Number(process.env.LOCAL_MODEL_TIMEOUT ?? 180_000);
const TEMPERATURE = 0.4; const MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS = 1024;
```
It runs the **real production prompts** (`convex/agentPrompts.ts` `buildSystemPrompt`/`buildUserPrompt`, `convex/agentTools.ts` `buildQuoteTools`, `src/utils/personas.ts`) with and without tools, counts tool calls rather than assuming them (line 124: *"decides whether free mode needs a…"*), and line 377 notes it exercises *"the path free mode would actually ship."* Outputs `evals/local-model-scores.json` / `local-model-runs.json`. Also `LFM2.5-2.6B` appears as a test fixture in `src/utils/ai-client-reasoning.test.ts:81`.

Sibling harnesses in `evals/`: `run-apparatus.ts` (apparatus-specific), `run-extract.ts` (target extraction), plus `run-interview`, `run-rubric`, `run-robustness`, `run-experiment`, `judge.ts`, `llm-client.ts`, with datasets `apparatus.jsonl`, `extract.jsonl`, `dataset.jsonl`.

---

## How it all connects

```
editor/index.tsx  ──onDraftChanged(45s debounce)──┐
selection popup "Get sources" ──researchSelection─┤
editorial-board-overlay ──steerBackgroundResearch─┤
                                                  ▼
                        src/utils/background-research.ts  (the engine)
                                                  │
              1. runClientResearchExtract  ──► ai-client.ts (writer's own model, BYOK)
                 prompts from research-targets.ts  ──► ResearchTarget[]
              2. selectFreshTargets (dedupe vs bibliography + TTL + session keys)
              3. searchForTarget ──► switch (settings.researchProvider):
                    "search-api"        ► research-backends.ts ► TinyFish/Exa/Tavily/Brave/Serper/custom
                    "model-web-search"  ► ai-client.runClientResearchWebSearch
                    "web-mcp"           ► mcp-research.searchMcpServers
                    "hosted" / fallback ► convex/research.ts searchSources (env-selected, TinyFish default)
              4. rankSourcesForTarget (heuristic, no embeddings)
              5. persistTarget ──► bibliography.ts ──► Lix /bibliography.json ──► Convex bibliographyEntries
              6. notify() ──► "twyne:background-research" / "twyne:background-sources"
                                                  ▼
                      citations-panel.tsx (in-editor "Deep Trace") + routes/apparatus/index.tsx
```

Key gates: no configured AI provider ⇒ no auto-research at all (extraction is AI-only); `provider === "local"` from Convex is rejected as evidence; every persisted background entry carries `provenance: "background"`, `accepted: false`, and a `target` back-ref so the panel can show *why* it was found and let the writer accept or drop it.

**Gaps relevant to what you're likely planning:** no vector/semantic layer anywhere, no local document corpus (only MCP resources as a remote knowledge base, text-only, 20k chars), and `convex/research.ts fetchSource` (URL → clean markdown, with `embeddable`) exists server-side but appears unused from the client — that's the natural hook if you want to pull full source text on-device.
